  - Utilize LLC 0’s Multimodal IBCI API to integrate data from multiple modalities (EEG, fNIRS, MEG) for a holistic neural map.
  - Employ LLC 1’s Decoded Neurofeedback Facility to train the agent in real-time neurofeedback, enhancing their ability to modulate neural patterns for encoding intent and cognitive states.[](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11861396/)
  - Record longitudinal data on cognitive functions, memory, and decision-making patterns using LLC 4’s Multimodal Neurodata Server.
  - Store neural data in a DNA-based storage system (LLC 5) for long-term preservation, leveraging its high-density and durability.[](https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/science/articles/10.3389/fsci.2023.1017235/full)
- **Technologies**:
  - High-density electrode arrays (e.g., CorTec’s °AirRay Electrodes) for recording and stimulation.[](https://cortec-neuro.com/applications/brain-computer-interface-bci/)
  - AI-driven decoding algorithms (e.g., LLC 1: DecNef INT4-INT8-FP16 Optimal Matrix) to extract behavioral variables and mental states.
  - Time-frequency analysis (e.g., Wavelet Transform, STFT) for capturing dynamic neural signals.[](https://www.nexstem.ai/)
- **Challenges**:
  - Ensuring signal fidelity and minimizing invasiveness.[](https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S2667325824001559)
  - Ethical concerns regarding continuous neural monitoring and data privacy.[](https://journals.plos.org/plosbiology/article?id=10.1371/journal.pbio.3002899)

