- **Cognitive Liberty**: Protect the agent’s right to cognitive sovereignty, using LLC 6’s soulbound neurotokens to prevent unauthorized access or manipulation.
- **Regulatory Compliance**: Align with international guidelines (e.g., OECD, UNESCO) for neurotechnology ethics.[](https://journals.plos.org/plosbiology/article?id=10.1371/journal.pbio.3002899)
- **Existential Risks**: Address philosophical questions about the nature of the reanimated entity (e.g., is it a true continuation of the original consciousness?).

## Technical Limitations
- **Signal Fidelity**: Current BCIs struggle with noise and limited resolution, impacting the accuracy of neural mapping.[](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8286886/)
- **Scalability**: Organoid intelligence and ASI systems require significant advancements to replicate complex human cognition.[](https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/science/articles/10.3389/fsci.2023.1017235/full)
- **Latency**: Achieving zero-latency telepresence remains a challenge, despite LLC 3’s advancements.
- **Data Security**: Post-quantum cryptography and zero-knowledge proofs are still maturing, posing risks to neural data integrity.

